    "Normal" : {

    },
    "Normal can be made impossible to bypass. Instructions are in Normal's Settings > FAQ." : {
      "comment" : "A note in the onboarding finish view that describes the security of the app.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Normal identifies an NFC tag by its unique ID, not by the data stored inside it." : {
      "comment" : "A description of how NFC tags are handled by the app.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Normal is 100% free with no in-app purchases, subscriptions, or hidden fees. It's an open-source project and the source code is available on GitHub for you to modify and tinker with." : {

    },
    "Normal is free and open-source, and always will be. No paywalls, subscriptions, ads or data-collection. If you would like to support Normal, donations are greatly appreciated." : {
      "comment" : "A paragraph explaining the benefits of supporting Normal.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Normal needs camera access to scan QR code and barcode keys. Enable camera access for Normal in Settings." : {
      "comment" : "A description of why the user needs to enable camera access in order to use the app.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Normal needs Screen Time access. Open Normal to allow it." : {
      "comment" : "Error message when Screen Time access is not authorized.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Normal only reads the tag's unique ID, never the data on it. That means only the tag you register can unblock your apps, and your privacy stays protected." : {

    },
    "Normal reads the value inside the QR code or barcode. Use something you can recreate later if you lose it, or make it random so it's hard to reproduce." : {
      "comment" : "Bullet point in the \"Where to place them\" card explaining that even if you make it hard to reach the keys, it will be hard to unblock your device. Also includes a footnote with more information.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Normal uses Apple's Screen Time API and the Managed Settings framework to enforce app limits entirely on your device. All blocking rules, schedules, and configurations are stored locally, nothing is ever sent to a server." : {

    },
    "Normal uses Screen Time to block and unblock apps. You can grant this now or later, it's required to select and block apps." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the Screen Time permission feature.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Normal works fully offline. No internet connection is required to set up or enforce your screen time limits." : {

    },
    "Now you have a dumb phone with iPhone hardware, the best of both worlds." : {

    },
